ess/mage-the-ascension/1346106-book-of-the-fallen-discussion?p=1346781#post1346781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Backers are &quot;supposed&quot; to get their pdf for errata &quot;this week&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Penelope was asking for when the book would be for sale on DRPG. That's not what the backer copies are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T11:41:50-08:00","id":1346795,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4418_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4418\" data-vbnamecard=\"4418\">tasti man LH</a> thank you. I didn't back the Kickstarter (I think it was years ago).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T15:59:24-08:00","id":1346886,"title":"","content":"It is available (for backers)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T17:23:53-08:00","id":1346902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1346106-book-of-the-fallen-discussion?p=1346770#post1346770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, just as a reminder, Brucato's take on nephandi is to deliberately push away from &quot;moustache-twirling infernalist&quot; and to focus more on human evils. That the former he always considered to be a boring and shallow take on that faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>my own feelings are mixed, because I liked them as cartoonish world annihilationists AND AS A DISTRACTION. The real evil were the selfish narcissists, or fanatic zealots, among the Traditions and Technocrats who reflected human evils writ large by virtue of what their abilities made them capable of. The comparatively alien threat of the Nephandi was always more flamboyant but did less real harm in the long run. They were the threat that led to witchhunts that did far more harm than they ever could.<br /> <br /> But Brucato making them the central threat of M20 meant making them more humanly evil rather was absolutely the right call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-09-2019, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T18:32:45-08:00","id":1346910,"title":"","content":"Holy fuck, the foreword and afterword are <i>powerful</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T20:04:47-08:00","id":1346929,"title":"","content":"So.....<br /> <br /> Is it good or what","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T23:06:07-08:00","id":1346949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jihelu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1346106-book-of-the-fallen-discussion?p=1346929#post1346929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.....<br /> <br /> Is it good or what</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm only a couple dozen pages in and... I don't know. I'd call it dark. Interesting. Grim. I think it's well written so far, so if that's your litmus test, it's good. Otherwise, the content is the very opposite of good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/753-ariketh","name":"Ariketh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T23:31:07-08:00","id":1346950,"title":"","content":"I'm still working my way through, and it's entirely possible (likely, even) that I've missed something. That said:<br /> <br /> I have a game system concern regarding Innocuous Aura: you pay 5 Merit points to be <i>just like someone who isn't a Nephandus</i>?<br /> <br /> As well, I'm wondering if there's a non-Fallen counterpart to Abyssal Mastery, something that, say, a Dreamspeaker or a Lion of Zion could use: the former to visit the Deep Umbra without risking Disembodiment, and the latter for access to the Sephiroth (if the Qlippoth are real, it implies that the Sephiroth are as well). <br /> <br /> I'm inclined to scrap Abyssal Lunatic, and instead reconceptualize Morbidity (at least for Nephandi) as a \u201cdegrees of Abyssal Lunacy\u201d trait, with the maximum level being equivalent to the Abyssal Lunatic Flaw found in the book. Frankly, \u201cthis Flaw makes the character unplayable\u201d doesn't work for me: if the character is such a raving lunatic that he's unplayable, he's a far better match for Morbidity 6 than for a Supernatural Flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T00:05:03-08:00","id":1346954,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25315\" data-vbnamecard=\"25315\">Jihelu</a><br /> Give it time. This is a LOOOOOOOOOT of text to read. Seriously. 200 pages. Don't expect an in-depth by-chapter review soon unless somebody spends the whole day reading it all. I'm also working my way through, still. I've not reached some of the Merit stuff that Aleph's already in, and I gotta head to work soon, But here's what I have so far:<br /> <br /> It's the first 20th book with a big, fat &quot;Content Warning, you can turn back&quot; right at the beginning, and it's deserved. ArcaneArts is also right that foreword alone is a punch, and give a bit of insight on where parts of the books are coming from.<br /> <br /> I'll say this outright though, Dwayne had it half right - in the way that the book is filled with everything, from absolute horrific, gut-wrenching real-world evils taking place right now to the absolute fantastic lovecraftian horror style Nephandi. It's the whole range, and it doesn't pull punches at all. Some people might not want part of that range in their entertainment.<br /> As a sidebar in the book states that, If we're talking about how to use the book in a M20 game, you really need to carefully pick which flavor of Nephandic evil you want to toss against your players - because not every kind of evil described in the book might make for a good time at the table.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, this is a M20 book. It gives you Nephandi lore in gargantuan buckets - from details about the cauls, to more about Qlippothic spheres, Nephandi mindsets, history, big players, the whole works. But it also ranges from the Nephandi groups we all know with their demons and otherworldly masters and infernals and cliche villans, to new(ly revelead) Nephadi types and groups that do their Descension through very very real, non-mustache-twirling, non-demonic-cliche things - and it's not written in any edgy way, which makes it <i>heavier</i>.<br /> I can absolutely see why this book took as long as it did.<br /> <br /> It's hard to say if it is a &quot;Good&quot; book, because with this thing here? It really depends on what you are looking for when you say &quot;Good&quot;. If you are just looking for a typical &quot;Fun antagonists for your game!&quot; book, then no, it isn't good. It has that with the typical Nephandic cliche groups, but the other half are not &quot;Fun&quot; Antagonists.<br /> <br /> So far I think the book is fantastic for what it is and tries to be, and exactly because it goes through the whole range of evil and the whole range of depictions of evil without holding back, and I don't mind reading it.<br /> But this is really, really not light material. If you use it for a M20 game as an ST, pick what parts you want to make use of, and be ware of the group at your table or online game. Seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 11-08-2019, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T00:10:05-08:00","id":1346956,"title":"","content":"From what I've heard so far: It's some good stuff.<br /> <br /> Are qlippothic spheres just a reflavor or are their mechanical bonuses? I don't need/want extreme details but I recall one book basically just said &quot;Qlippothic 